  "body": "Sale Method - Deadline Private Treaty: Closes 2:00 p.m. Thursday 21 January 2027 (unless sold prior)\r\n\r\nStep into a world where master boatbuilding heritage, architectural brilliance, and eco-conscious modern luxury collide. Tucked away in exclusive Stanley Point, 33 Glen Road is a private sanctuary, a multi-generational haven, and a coastal lifestyle beyond compare. \r\n\r\nThe CV does not reflect the quality of the renovations or the presentation of the property, this truly is something to be experienced in person.\r\n\r\nA classic 1910 villa, has been extensively transformed by renowned heritage architect Stephen Jones (formerly of Salmond Reed Architects). This expansive six-bedroom home effortlessly bridges the charm of the early 1900s with state-of-the-art 21st-century comfort. The home which now has been effectively fully rebuilt incorporates a high standard of specification and finishing throughout and benefits from good indoor/outdoor flow to associated balconies and patio/timber decked areas. The 2013 renovation developed the entrance, and main living facilities and garaging, along with the new separate two bedroom suite to the lower level, with the 2016 structural addition of the master suite to the top of the house, with new roof and integrated services. \r\n\r\nKEY HIGHLIGHTS & ARCHITECTURAL FEATURES:\r\nThe architectural project included replacement of the original timber piles, creation of the concrete and block basement and substantial structural steel strengthening through the middle and upper levels. Extensive thermal insulation was installed within the walls, with additional acoustic insulation between the basement and main level and beneath the principal ensuite and a ducted air conditioning and heating system throughout.\r\n\r\nThis substantial residence home offers six bedrooms across three levels, all with built-in wardrobes, providing flexibility for families of all ages. Three bedrooms are on the main level, including a private double ensuite with bifold doors opening to a secluded, flower-filled courtyard with a retractable sun awning, ideal for au pairs, visiting family or guests. \r\n\r\nThe whole new upper-level is dedicated to the principal suite, created by raising the roofline, includes an ensuite and dressing room, with breathtaking views towards Auckland city in one direction and Ngataringa Bay in the other. Peaceful and private, it provides an adult retreat from the activity of family life.\r\n\r\nAt the heart of the main living area, the large and thoughtfully planned family kitchen connects naturally with the dining area, living room with its log burner and pressed-tin feature wall and outdoor spaces. Large sliding doors open to the main deck, while two additional side doors provide direct access to further decked areas, creating an effortless setting for everyday family life and entertaining. Appliances include a mains-gas hob and double electric ovens, one with steam functionality. The self-contained lower ground floor with acoustic dampening includes two bedrooms, a bathroom and a compact kitchenette. It can serve as a media room, children’s breakout space, teenage retreat, guest suite or private accommodation for extended family, giving the home genuine multi-generational flexibility. \r\n\r\nYou have direct park and water access, with a private bridge at the foot of your garden which leads straight into Stanley Bay Park and Ngataringa Bay for kayaking, paddleboarding, or a calm swim; local moorings and jetties available.\r\n\r\nDon’t miss the opportunity to own property in one of Auckland’s most coveted coastal enclaves. \r\n\r\n*Holders of an Active Investor Plus (AIP) visa are invited to view; however, any purchase will be subject to Overseas Investment Office (OIO) approval.\r\n\r\nPlease contact Amanda Evans at New Zealand Sotheby's International Realty for more information.",
